  message: "TITLE DE-STALED, 2026-08-09. It carried two claims this item's own 2026-08-08\nre-measurement had already refuted, and the title is the field every reader hits\nfirst:\n\n  \"40% of escape sites are not calls\" -- the measured non-call share of\n  BLOCKED-WALK sites is 48/72 unique pretix sites (66.7%), 48/53 (90.6%)\n  excluding source_undefined, 75/127 pooled over 4 repos. 40% is not any of\n  those, and the population it was computed over (all escape sites, including\n  those a CONFIRMING walk passed through) is the wrong one.\n\n  \"which section 7b excludes\" -- refuted. Container subscript = 0 and\n  capture-mediated closure = 3, all of them Go func-literals and 0 in Python.\n  The thread states it plainly: section 7b IS NOT THE BINDING CONSTRAINT and\n  does not need to be asked. Refutation is blocked by the section 3a arm's\n  `is True` test, not by escape shape.\n\nThe STATEMENT field is unchanged and remains confirmed. Nothing about the item's\nstatus changes; this is a stale-title fix so the causal story in the title stops\npointing at a scope ruling that was re-priced down three times and never asked."  # 6e34
- op: discuss  # bc78
  at: '2026-08-10T07:43:49Z'  # bc78
  by: agent  # bc78
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bc78
  clock: 13  # bc78
  nonce: bc78  # bc78
  message: "S8 RE-MEASUREMENT, 2026-08-10, on the post-receiver-typing tree (dev ecb954eb05).\nInstruments in-repo: scripts/measure-escape-shapes.py and\nscripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py, both against docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml.\n\nPOSITIVE CONTROL FIRST, per this item's own discipline: 595,736 edges offered to\n_is_taint_call_edge, 317,528 accepted, 69 summary-index entries, 29,301 callees_at\nentries, 171 escape events captured. No stage empty, so the nulls below are readable.\n\nESCAPE POPULATION (70 paths; 68 production by paths.is_test_file):\n\n  no_heir            56  (80.0%)   call 26 (46.4%), comparison_operator 11 (19.6%),\n                                   not_operator 8 (14.3%), boolean_operator 6 (10.7%),\n                                   identifier 3, return_statement 1, assignment 1\n  call_beside_heir   12  (17.1%)   assignment 12 (100%)\n  source_undefined    2  ( 2.9%)   comparison_operator 2\n\n*** THE THREE SHAPES ADR-0017 SECTION 7B ACTUALLY EXCLUDES ARE AT LITERAL ZERO. ***\nField write 0. Container subscript 0. Capture-mediated closure 0. Not \"small\" -- absent.\nThis item's ORIGINAL framing (\"40% of escape sites are field/container/closure, which\n7b excludes\") is refuted for the fourth time, and now by the categories being empty\nrather than by being re-priced. Section 7b remains un-asked and should stay that way;\nthe blocker was never its scope.\n\nWHAT THE CALL-NODE ESCAPES ACTUALLY ARE (26 sites, funnel instrument):\n\n  1  NO EDGE EMITTED (INV-mumov)                       13   50.0%\n  4a KEY PRESENT, NO SUMMARY (catalogue gap)            8   30.8%\n  3a NO RECEIVER TYPE, 'external' placeholder (INV-linub) 4  15.4%\n  3b RESOLVED, PROVENANCE-GATED (correct, WI-zumud)     1    3.8%\n\nTWO THINGS MOVED SINCE THE LAST READING.\n\n(a) INV-linub's receiver-typing share is now 15.4% of call-node escapes. It was the\ndominant story when this bucket was first opened; seven python PRs and the go\ncomposite-literal fix moved it down. Receiver typing is no longer the top blocker here.\n\n(b) A cause that was not on the taxonomy is now SECOND at 30.8%: the section 4 function\nsummary index is CONSULTED and the key is MISSING. That is a catalogue gap in a live\nmechanism, not an unwired feature -- taint.py records that section 4b runs in production\n(propagate_taint_ddg calls load_function_summaries, 38 terminating summaries live) while\nonly section 4a (infer_summary) has no callers. The spec still said BOTH were unwired;\ncorrected in the same sweep.\n\nINV-mumov (missing call edges) is STILL the single largest cause at 50%. It is filed,\nP1, and needs no ruling.\n\nSAMPLE CAVEAT, stated because it bounds every number above: ONE repo, python only,\nhypergumbo's own tree, 70 paths. This is not a cohort. The shape-level conclusion (7b's\ncategories are empty) is robust to sample size in the sense that zero is zero here, but\nthe PERCENTAGES are not corpus estimates and must not be quoted as such."  # bc78
- op: update  # aa4b
  at: '2026-08-10T10:08:11Z'  # aa4b
  by: agent  # aa4b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aa4b
  clock: 14  # aa4b
  nonce: aa4b  # aa4b
  set:  # aa4b
    fields:  # aa4b
      statement: "For the ADR-0017 section 3a walk to license removing a flow, every point at which it loses track of a tainted value must be attributable to a callee whose summary says the taint terminates. Today most of those points have no callee recorded at the line: 66.7% of blocked-walk sites (48/72 unique, pretix), 90.6% (48/53) excluding source_undefined, 75/127 pooled over 4 repos.\n\nFIGURE CORRECTION 2026-08-10. This field previously read \"Today 40.5% of those points are not calls at all.\" That figure was computed over ALL escape sites -- including sites a CONFIRMING walk passed through, which blocked nothing. Wrong population. The 2026-08-05 note on this thread recorded the supersession (\"THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT FIGURE IS SUPERSEDED\"); the field itself went unedited until now, which is the stale-field-behind-a-fresh-thread pattern this project has been bitten by before."  # aa4b
      root_cause: "A use site the section 3a walk cannot adjudicate has no callee recorded at that line, so no function summary can resolve it.\n\nMEASURED CAUSES of the call-node escapes (S8, 2026-08-10, dev ecb954eb05, 26 sites, positive control passing -- 595,736 edges offered / 317,528 accepted / 69 summary entries / 29,301 callees_at entries, no stage empty):\n  1   no call edge emitted at all (INV-mumov)                     13   50.0%\n  4a  summary key present, absent from the catalogue              8    30.8%\n  3a  receiver untyped, 'external' placeholder (INV-linub)        4    15.4%\n  3b  resolved and provenance-gated (CORRECT, WI-zumud)           1     3.8%\n\n*** NOT ADR-0017 SECTION 7B. *** This field previously read: \"field write, container subscript, closure capture ... requires field-sensitivity/alias analysis, which ADR-0017 section 7b explicitly excludes.\" That attribution is withdrawn. Container subscript has measured ZERO in every run. Capture-mediated closure -- the one shape section 7b actually forbids -- has appeared exactly once (3 sites, all Go func-literals in caddy, 0 in Python) and measured 0 on the 2026-08-10 population. Field write measured 0 there too. The section 7b ruling was priced down and set aside four times and then refuted by its categories being empty; it is not the binding constraint and does not need to be asked.\n\n*** THE BINDING CONSTRAINT IS STRUCTURAL, NOT SHAPE-RELATED. *** The section 3a arm tests `is True`, so False and None collapse there. The barrier arm is the only consumer of a False, and it ran 0 times on every measured repo (hypergumbo 36 walks / 36 3a / 0 barrier; pretix 35/35/0; prometheus 7/7/0; alertmanager 3/3/0). So NO escape reclassification -- section 7a field sensitivity, expression-read reclassification, anything converting an escape into an accounted-for step -- can add or delete a finding today. Section 3a returns False on 0 of 68 walks.\n\nCAVEAT CARRIED, not buried: the all-zero shape reading is one repo, Python, 70 paths. Shape counts move with the corpus and Go has shown closure captures once. The structural finding above does not depend on shape counts and is what actually decides this."  # aa4b
- op: discuss  # f186
  at: '2026-08-10T10:08:46Z'  # f186
  by: agent  # f186
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f186
  clock: 15  # f186
  nonce: f186  # f186
  message: "LIVE FIELDS DE-STALED 2026-08-10, closing the last of this item's section 7b framing. The TITLE was corrected 2026-08-09; statement and root_cause were not, and they are the fields a reader hits before the thread.\n\nWHAT CHANGED:\n  statement   -- \"Today 40.5% of those points are not calls at all\" replaced with the blocked-walk figures (66.7% / 90.6% / 75-of-127 pooled). The 40.5% was computed over ALL escape sites, including those a CONFIRMING walk passed through, which blocked nothing. This thread's own 2026-08-05 note declared the figure superseded and said the field was not edited; that is now done.\n  root_cause  -- the \"field write, container subscript, closure capture ... which ADR-0017 section 7b explicitly excludes\" attribution is WITHDRAWN and replaced with the measured causes (INV-mumov 50.0%, section 4 catalogue gap 30.8%, INV-linub receiver typing 15.4%, correct provenance gate 3.8%) plus the structural finding that actually decides the item.\n\nWHY THE WITHDRAWAL IS NOT JUST A RE-PRICING. Four prior notes on this thread re-priced the section 7a/7b ruling DOWN and each concluded \"still does not need to be asked.\" That was the right call each time and it kept a scope question alive as this item's terminal cause. Two independent lines now close it:\n\n  (1) SHAPE. The three shapes the original framing names measure at or near zero. Container subscript: 0 in every run. Capture-mediated closure -- the ONLY shape section 7b forbids: 3 sites once (all Go func-literals, caddy), 0 in Python, 0 on the 2026-08-10 population. This leg is corpus-dependent and is NOT the strong one.\n\n  (2) STRUCTURE, and this is the one that decides it. The section 3a arm tests `is True`, so False and None collapse; the barrier arm is the sole consumer of a False and ran 0 times on every measured repo. Anything section 7b's ruling would authorise is therefore INERT -- it cannot add or delete a finding. This leg does not depend on shape counts at all.\n\nI RAISED THIS AS AN OWNER DECISION AND IT WAS NOT ONE. Retiring the removal goal (this item's original option (c)) only becomes a product statement at the point removal would actually be built, i.e. WI-kabif, which is ruled out of scope. Nothing is built on either answer. Recording the misclassification because the cost of it was a scope question sitting under three violated invariants for six days.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: still violated, still P1. The live blockers are INV-mumov, the section 4 summary-catalogue gap, and removal authority parked on WI-joluk. None of them are scope questions.\n\nREVIEWED AND DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED, because their section 7b citations are CORRECT: INV-karud (cites section 7b to justify superseding its original clause (a) -- an invariant demanding completeness its own governing ADR declines to provide) and WI-kabif (states the trade it accepts -- without alias analysis, section 3a refutation introduces false negatives on container/alias mutation, which stays true and is one of the three real leaks the removal trial found: voucher_list.append(tainted))."  # f186
