  set:  # bf28
    description: "MEASURED BLOCKER, not a hypothesis. ADR-0017 section 4 function summaries are\nnow wired and the python/go catalogues cover every enumerated callee a\nqualified-name catalogue can express (PR #197), and section 3a still refutes\nNOTHING. The reason is this item.\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED (cohort: caddy, alertmanager, pretix, kserve, zoxide):\n  264 escape sites where the section 3a walk lost track of a tainted value\n   107 (40.5%)  NO CALL AT THE LINE AT ALL\n    64 (24.2%)  callee module unresolved (external.*)\n    26 ( 9.8%)  first-party in-repo callee\n    67 (25.4%)  stdlib/third-party -- a declared catalogue can name these\n    25 ( 9.5%)  ...and of those, actually terminate the taint\n\n  A/B on the same binary, catalogue live vs forced empty:\n    16 confirmed / 40 unknown / 0 refuted -- IDENTICAL in both arms.\n\nWHY 25 CLOSED SITES BUY ZERO FLOWS. A walk returns unknown if ANY branch\nescapes, so a flow becomes refutable only when EVERY escape on it closes. Of\n37 unknown walks, 5 did close at least one site and every one of them still\nhad another open. Per-walk anatomy of what held them open:\n    81  no call at line\n    40  catalogued but propagates\n    21  callee module unresolved\n    12  uncatalogued callee\nAnd at the margin -- the 14 walks held open by exactly ONE site, i.e. the ones\nnearest to refutable -- the single blocker is \"no call at the line\" in 10 of\n14. Fixing everything else on this list still would not refute those 10.\n\nWHAT \"NO CALL AT THE LINE\" MEANS. The tainted value is used at a line that\ndefines nothing the DDG tracked AND invokes nothing: a field write\n(self.x = tainted), a container subscript (d[k] = tainted), a closure capture.\nThere is no callee to look up, so no function summary can ever help. This is\nADR-0017 section 7a field-sensitivity / alias analysis territory, and section\n7b EXPLICITLY EXCLUDES alias analysis and whole-program analysis.\n\nTHIS WAS FILED AS A SCOPE COLLISION. IT IS NOT ONE -- REFUTED 2026-08-10; see\nthe live root_cause field and the thread. The paragraph below is kept as filed\nbecause the three options it enumerates are still the real option set, but its\npremise is withdrawn: the shapes section 7b excludes measure at or near zero,\nand refutation is blocked structurally (the section 3a arm tests `is True`, so\nFalse and None collapse, and the barrier arm -- the only consumer of a False --\nran 0 times on every measured repo). No escape reclassification can move a\nfinding today, so option (b) is inert rather than expensive, and section 7b\ndoes not need to be asked. AS FILED, PREMISE WITHDRAWN: Section 3a's removal\nauthority requires distinguishing \"the taint stopped here\" from \"I lost it\nhere\", and for 40% of escape sites that distinction needs precisely the\ncapability section 7b declines to build. Three honest options, none of them\nfree:\n  (a) Narrow refutation's DOMAIN: refute only flows whose every escape site is\n      a call with a catalogued terminating summary. Sound, and by this\n      measurement it addresses 0 of 51 walks today -- so it would ship as an\n      inert capability unless the other blockers move first.\n  (b) Implement enough field-sensitivity to track a value into a field or\n      container slot within one function (section 7a is \"field-sensitivity\n      LITE\" and already partially exists). Reopens the section 7b line.\n  (c) Accept confirm-only permanently and RETIRE the removal goal, updating\n      WI-kabif and INV-sadah to match what the analysis can actually do.\nDo not pick one from the armchair -- (b)'s size is unmeasured, and that\nmeasurement is the next step for this item.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR ADJACENT ITEMS, stated so they are not closed on this PR:\n * INV-sadah stays violated. Its statement requires INCLUSION be decided by\n   data-dependence information; the walk still only CONFIRMS.\n * WI-kabif stays todo_hard. Its filed list of four prerequisites was already\n   six (section 4 summaries, per-call-site lines); this was filed as the\n   SEVENTH, \"not a wiring gap but a declared scope exclusion\" -- WITHDRAWN\n   2026-08-10. It is not a scope exclusion and not a prerequisite; WI-kabif's\n   own section 7b citation (false negatives on container/alias mutation) is a\n   separate and still-correct statement of a trade it accepts."  # bf28
- op: discuss  # fd61
  at: '2026-08-10T20:09:39Z'  # fd61
  by: agent  # fd61
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fd61
  clock: 17  # fd61
  nonce: fd61  # fd61
  message: "CEILING MEASURED 2026-08-10 (dev 52acec99be). The structural finding this item\nalready carries is now measured at its UPPER BOUND rather than argued, and the\ninstrument is in-repo: scripts/measure-escape-closing-ceiling.py.\n\nTHE METHOD, and why a ceiling rather than an increment. Every open proposal in\nthis family closes escape sites -- the 4a catalogue gap, INV-mumov's missing\nemission, INV-linub's untyped receivers. An increment measured at zero cannot be\ntold apart from an instrument that cannot see (this repo has produced that\nreading four times). So the arm forces _use_site_terminates to return True\nunconditionally: EVERY escape site closes at once, which no catalogue, emission\nor receiver-typing fix can exceed.\n\nINSTRUMENT CONTROL PASSED FIRST: 16 walks left `none` in the ceiling arm, so the\npatch is demonstrably on the path the walk takes.\n\n  hypergumbo, docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml\n    _use_site_terminates calls        160 / 160\n    3a walks  True/False/None   (A)   22 /  0 / 20\n    3a walks  True/False/None   (B)   22 / 16 /  4\n    barrier walks / False       (A)    0 / 0      (B)  0 / 0\n    FINDINGS violated/sanitized/evidence\n                                (A)    2 / 1453 / 2279\n                                (B)    2 / 1453 / 2279\n    DELTA                              0 /    0 /    0\n\n*** CLOSING EVERY ESCAPE SITE MOVED 16 WALKS None->False AND ZERO FINDINGS. ***\n\nWHY IT CANNOT BE OTHERWISE, read in code and confirmed at unit level. `summaries`\nhas exactly one consumer chain -- _qualified_callee -> _catalogue_key_for_edge ->\ncallees_at -> _use_site_terminates -- and it only ever decides `continue` vs\n`escaped = True`; it never adds a frontier entry. The walk returns True at\n`if uses & targets: return True` BEFORE any escape is considered. So closing an\nescape can only convert None -> False. Unit probe, control escape firing first:\n\n    control  verdict None (escape at line 5, no_heir)\n    ceiling  verdict False\n    3a arm      `is True`  : False -> False   UNCHANGED (inert)\n    barrier arm `is False` : False -> True    MOVED -> earns `sanitized`\n\nHONEST LIMITS. (1) Barrier walks were 0 in BOTH arms here, so the suppressive\ndirection is UNEXERCISED on this repo, not disproven -- the unit probe shows it\nfires wherever the barrier arm runs. (2) One repo, python. The 3a inertness is\nstructural and does not depend on the corpus; the barrier-arm magnitude does.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE 4a BUCKET, which is also MISNAMED. Its 8 sites carry 7\ndistinct keys and only 4 are catalogue absences (os.makedirs, subprocess.run,\nos.path.join, os.path.dirname). The other 3 are defects of a different kind:\n`sys.sys.stderr` and `os.os.path` have a DOUBLED module segment -- the analyzer\nputs a module-qualified name in the NAME slot and _qualified_callee concatenates\nmodule + \".\" + name anyway -- and `file.write` carries a receiver variable in the\nmodule slot. No catalogue entry can match a malformed key. Filed separately.\n\nBEARING ON THIS ITEM'S STATUS: unchanged, still violated. The measurement does\nnot satisfy the statement; it prices the remedy at zero findings and shows the\nonly direction available is the suppressive one."  # fd61
- op: discuss  # 3f34
  at: '2026-08-17T00:18:52Z'  # 3f34
  by: agent  # 3f34
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3f34
  clock: 18  # 3f34
  nonce: 3f34  # 3f34
  message: "LIVE root_cause FIELD CARRIES A REFUTED CLAIM. Recorded here rather than edited\nin place, because the surrounding structural argument is sound and only its\nload-bearing premise moved. 2026-08-16, dev 80bbba4be7.\n\nTHE CLAIM, quoted from the live root_cause field: \"The barrier arm is the only\nconsumer of a False, and it ran 0 times on every measured repo (hypergumbo 36\nwalks / 36 3a / 0 barrier; pretix 35/35/0; prometheus 7/7/0; alertmanager\n3/3/0). So NO escape reclassification -- section 7a field sensitivity,\nexpression-read reclassification, anything converting an escape into an\naccounted-for step -- can add or delete a finding today.\"\n\nTHE BARRIER ARM RUNS. A/B on ONE repo, ONE binary, ONE variable changed\n(instrument: production _ddg_taint_reaches wrapped, every call tallied by arm):\n\n    alertmanager, no sanitizer for the flow's label    34 walks,  0 barrier\n    alertmanager, + 9 laundering fns as sanitizers     55 walks, 21 barrier\n\nWHY THE ZERO WAS AN ARTEFACT. The barrier arm needs barrier_sites non-empty for\nthe (source_fn, taint_label) pair, i.e. a sanitizer declared for THAT LABEL,\ncalled in the SAME function as the source. The built-in sanitizer catalogue\nexpresses exactly two transforms -- plaintext -> ciphertext and key_material ->\nderived_key -- so under the default catalogue a flow carrying any other label\nCANNOT be reported sanitized and the arm is unreachable BY CONSTRUCTION, on\nevery repo, forever. The measured zeros were measuring the catalogue, not the\ncode path. The run's own stderr says as much and was the tell: \"A flow whose\ntaint label is not one of those CANNOT be reported sanitized, so a zero there\nmeans not expressible, not not protected.\" The population was \"repos analysed\nwith the default sanitizer catalogue\", stated as \"every measured repo\".\n\nThe 9 probe sanitizers were ordinary laundering functions (net/url.QueryEscape,\nhtml.EscapeString, path/filepath.Clean, strings.TrimSpace, strconv.Quote, ...) --\na realistic --taint-sanitizers / extra_catalogs configuration, which is the\nconfiguration hypergumbo's own claims file uses and which the docs instruct\nusers to supply. So this is the ordinary user path, not an exotic one.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT OVERTURN.\n  DOES: the inference \"no escape reclassification can add or delete a finding\n  today\" holds only under the default sanitizer catalogue. For a project that\n  declares sanitizers, converting an escape into an accounted-for step can turn\n  a barrier None into a barrier False, and a barrier False earns sanitized and\n  DROPS the flow from the claim's violation set (PR #214). Escape\n  reclassification has teeth exactly where this field says it has none -- and\n  they cut toward DELETING findings, which is the unsafe direction.\n  DOES NOT: the shape measurements (66.7-90.6% of blocked-walk sites are\n  non-calls; the ADR-0017 7b categories measuring at or near zero; the S8 cause\n  breakdown) are untouched. The withdrawal of the 7b attribution stands.\n\nCROSS-REFERENCE. The same refutation is recorded on INV-lupav, whose 2026-08-08\nentry carries the identical \"0 production barrier walks have ever been observed\"\nclaim and whose stated closure criterion depended on it. Also measured there:\nacross 85 default-catalogue production walks on two repos and two languages the\nwalk returned False ZERO times, and with the barrier arm reachable (21 walks)\nstill zero. So refutation is blocked by a second, independent fact this item\nalready explains -- False requires exhaustion, and escapes dominate.\n\nSUGGESTED FIELD EDIT, not applied: the root_cause paragraph should say the arm\nis unreachable UNDER THE DEFAULT SANITIZER CATALOGUE, and name that as the\nreason, rather than reporting per-repo zeros that read as a property of the\ncode. Left to whoever next works this item, per the stale-field-behind-a-\nfresh-thread pattern this item has already been bitten by once."  # 3f34
